        title: "Screen-space LOD and refinement phases",
        question: "How does the renderer decide which supersamples need computation?",
        answer: "LOD accepts a block only when its sample evidence establishes a uniform interior or bounded exterior approximation within a screen-space threshold. Progressive rendering evaluates preview, sparse and dense phases; rejected blocks retain fully computed fallback samples.",
